    "description": "The Brief Sexual Attitudes Scale (BSAS) is a 23-item self-report questionnaire measuring individual attitudes toward sexuality across dimensions such as permissiveness, birth control, communalism, and instrumentality. It is used to characterize sexual value orientations in research on human sexuality and relationships.",
